### C. installAgents helper

Read: `coding-playbook/architecture/folder-structure`, `coding-playbook/services/service-layer`, `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`
- [ ] **Create `src/tools/init/installAgents/index.ts`** — Default export: `async function installAgents(agentDir: string, displayPrefix?: string): Promise<InitStepResult[]>`. Follows the exact same pattern as `installMethodologyDocs`: create target directory, iterate `listAgents()`, for each entry check if file exists (report `exists`), read content via `readCanonicalDoc` (report `skipped` on failure), write file and report `created`. The `agentDir` is the host's `.claude/agents` directory (absolute path). The `displayPrefix` defaults to `"agents"` for display names like `agents/aide/aide-spec-writer`. Each agent file is written to `join(agentDir, entry.hostFilename)` — the `aide/` subfolder is part of the `hostFilename`, so `mkdir` must be called with `{ recursive: true }` on the dirname of each target path to ensure the `aide/` subfolder exists.

